.TH TERMNAV-RELAY 1
.SH NAME
termnav-relay \- route navigation through nested SSH and tmux scopes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termnav-relay send
.I pane direction
[\fB--client-pid\fR \fIPID\fR]
.br
.B termnav-relay send
.I window next|previous
[\fB--client-pid\fR \fIPID\fR]
.br
.B termnav-relay send
.I move left|right
[\fB--client-pid\fR \fIPID\fR]
.br
.B termnav-relay ssh
[\fIssh arguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Termnav establishes one owner-only Unix socket forwarding channel on each
interactive SSH connection. Navigation requests are handled by the nearest
tmux scope and otherwise forwarded to its parent. The protocol contains only
fixed pane and window navigation operations.
.PP
Install \fBshare/termnav/sshd_config\fR as an sshd_config.d fragment on any
host that should participate, validate with \fBsshd -t\fR, and reload sshd.
.PP
Explicit SSH remote commands and non-session modes are passed to OpenSSH
unchanged. Participating SSH servers accept only TERMNAV_PARENT_RELAY from the
client environment. Failure to receive it makes navigation a silent no-op and
does not create another SSH connection or authentication attempt.
